>> title: Soy Sauce Chicken
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, chinese, soy sauce, poached, whole bird
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter, One Pot, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: see yao gai, si yau gai, 豉油雞, soya chicken, soy sauce chicken, lou sui gai
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — thirty-five minutes at a shiver and never a boil, or the skin splits and the breast dries while the thighs come up

>> step: simmer the lou sui 20 min
Simmer @water{8%cups}(1.9 L) with @light soy sauce{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL), @dark soy sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @Shaoxing wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @rock sugar{4%oz}(115 g), @star anise{3%pods}, @cassia bark{1%stick}, @dried tangerine peel{1%piece}, @fresh ginger{6%slices}(coin-sized) and @scallions{3}(knotted) in a #stockpot{} for ~simmer{20%min}, until the sugar has gone and the spices have opened.

>> step: poach 35 min at a shiver, turning twice
Poach @whole chicken{3 1/2%lb}(1.6 kg; rinsed and dried) breast-down in @&(~1)master stock{} for ~poach{35%min}, the surface never past a shiver, turning it twice.

>> step: rest in the pot 20 min, brush with sesame oil, chop
Rest @&(~1)chicken{} in the pot off the heat for ~rest{20%min}, lift it out to drain, brush it with @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}, and chop it through the bone into pieces to serve.

Strain the lou sui and keep it. Chill it lift the fat off and boil it up every few days topping up soy and sugar.
